The values is a list of 2, 3, 4, 6, 5, 7, 4, 1, 8, and 3.
The starts is a list of 0, 1, 3, and 6.
The success as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared valueslist as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 2 into valueslist.
Place 3 into valueslist.
Place 4 into valueslist.
Place 6 into valueslist.
Place 5 into valueslist.
Place 7 into valueslist.
Place 4 into valueslist.
Place 1 into valueslist.
Place 8 into valueslist.
Place 3 into valueslist.
Keep a shared startslist as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 0 into startslist.
Place 1 into startslist.
Place 3 into startslist.
Place 6 into startslist.
The dp is a list of 10 zeros.
For every spot from 6 to 9.
Set item spot of dp to item spot of valueslist.

The rows is a list of 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, and 0.
The columns is a list of 0, 1, 2, 0, 1, and 0.
For every step from 0 to 5.
The row is item step of rows.
The column is item step of columns.
The base is item row of startslist.
The below is item (row plus 1) of startslist.
The here is item (base plus column) of valueslist.
The first is item (below plus column) of dp.
The second is item (below plus column plus 1) of dp.
The small is first.
If second is less than small, set small to second.
Set item (base plus column) of dp to here plus small.

Show item 0 of dp.
